    "result": "`shipping_cost` is implemented in `solution.py` and follows all seven rules in `spec.md`. The 9 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass. I didn't run a coverage report, so I haven't confirmed the 90% line-coverage gate. The tests exercise every branch, so I expect it to pass.\n\nThe tests cover weight rounding, volumetric weight, the zone factors, free shipping, the oversize surcharge, float and `Decimal` inputs, and the `TypeError`/`ValueError` cases.\n\nThe spec doesn't say what to do with NaN or infinite inputs, so I made them raise `ValueError`.\n\nMy first run had one failing test, which was a wrong expectation in the test (I had miscalculated a volumetric weight), not a bug in the solution. I corrected the test.",
